cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: ".claude: the agent configuration for the weftspun workspace"
abstract: >
  Claude Code's workspace configuration for weftspun, kept as a repo project checked
  out at .claude/ rather than as a symlink or a file on one machine. It holds the
  working agreements that apply across every project on the hexagon -- the hard
  constraints on compute, archive formats, normal form, data hygiene and skinning, how
  measurements are reported, how a gate is verified, and the corpus blocklists -- and
  the settings that decide what an agent may do without asking. Both are tracked,
  reviewed and visible to repo status, so a widened permission arrives as a diff with a
  commit behind it. The per-machine half stays untracked. The record of what was
  measured and what was retracted is in weftspun/logbook; this repository holds what
  applies going forward.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/weftspun/dot-claude"
keywords:
  - claude-code
  - agent-configuration
  - repo-manifest

# Configuration for a tool, so what it is built on is the tool's format rather than any
# code. There is nothing vendored and nothing linked.
references:

  - type: software
    title: "Claude Code"
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic
    url: "https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code"
    notes: >
      The agent this configures. It reads `.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/settings.json`
      at the workspace root and merges `settings.local.json` over the second with local
      winning, which is why those two are separate files and why only the first is
      tracked. That it reads `.claude/` and nothing else is what fixes this project's
      `path` and forced the repository name to `dot-claude` instead.

  - type: software
    title: "repo: a tool built on top of Git for managing many repositories"
    authors:
      - name: "The Android Open Source Project"
    url: "https://gerrit.googlesource.com/git-repo"
    notes: >
      What puts this at `.claude/`. `_CheckLocalPath` bans only `.`, `..`, `.git` and
      `.repo*` as path components, so a leading-dot path is legal and gets an ordinary
      managed checkout with its gitdir under `.repo/projects/`. It is also why this
      repository exists: repo clones the manifest to `.repo/manifests`, so the CLAUDE.md
      that `meta` had left at the workspace root would have stopped being read.

  - type: software
    title: "weftspun: the repo manifest for the weftspun workspace"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/weftspun/weftspun"
    notes: >
      Where this file came from, and what places this repository at `.claude/`. It held
      the working agreements until the manifest was converted from meta to repo and the
      two jobs were told apart.

  - type: software
    title: "logbook: the weftspun engineering record"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/weftspun/logbook"
    notes: >
      The other half. `todo.md` carries the dated entries and the retractions kept beside
      what they retract, `PITFALLS.md` the recurring failure modes; every constraint in
      CLAUDE.md has an incident there behind it. A `linkfile` into it is what this
      repository was almost made from, and was refused because a symlink is invisible to
      `repo status`.

  - type: generic
    title: "ASD-STE100: Simplified Technical English"
    authors:
      - name: "AeroSpace and Defence Industries Association of Europe"
    url: "https://asd-ste100.org"
    notes: >
      The specification the writing rules in CLAUDE.md are measured against, and what
      `0-infrastructure/tropes-removal-model` gates prose in this workspace with.
